# Magmatic Hellkite: "Its controller searches" means the land's controller, not its owner. Bot2's Dack Fayden emblem ("Whenever
# you cast a spell that targets one or more permanents, gain control of those permanents") takes Bot1's Bazaar of Baghdad when Bot2
# casts Pyroblast at it (not blue, so Pyroblast does nothing else). On turn 13 Bot1's Hellkite destroys the Bazaar, which Bot2
# controls, so it is an opponent's nonbasic land and a legal target. The destroyed Bazaar goes to Bot1's graveyard (its owner's),
# while Bot2, the controller, searches its own library and gets a Forest, tapped with a stun counter. Bot1 searches nothing.

[Bot1 Deck]
Bazaar of Baghdad
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Magmatic Hellkite
Mountain
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Volcanic Island
Volcanic Island
Volcanic Island
Dack Fayden
Pyroblast
Forest
Forest
Forest x20

